/* The portrait, tone mapped for a dot screen rather than a character ramp:
   the range is pulled into the middle, because pure black leaves no paper
   between the dots and pure white leaves no dot at all. Kept at the photo's
   own framing rather than pre-cropped, so halftone.js can reproduce the same
   cover crop the <image> underneath performs and the two line up. Inlined
   because reading pixels back out of a canvas is blocked for a file:// image.
                                                                          */
window.PORTRAIT_SRC='data:image/jpeg;base64,';
